                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c46b9801-53c1-3769-a6e0-3a09ea48bfa5",
                        "entry_id": "7f4a23f1-9099-3b63-b6c8-9d86d811dd17",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne qui ne sait pas rire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d2af65d-14c3-48cb-847e-218c987b27ef",
                                "sense_id": "c46b9801-53c1-3769-a6e0-3a09ea48bfa5",
                                "text": "Aulcuns ont à l’Autheur reprouché de ne pas plus sçavoir le languaige du vieulx temps que les lièvres ne se cognoissent à faire des fagots. Iadis ces gens eussent esté nommez, à bon escient, cannibales, agelastes, sycophantes, voire mesmes ung peu yssus de la bonne ville de Gomorrhe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "765d3605-5855-4263-af0c-d58f2fd8445e",
                                "sense_id": "c46b9801-53c1-3769-a6e0-3a09ea48bfa5",
                                "text": "Lors de son passage dans l’espace cosmique, l’âme du véritable agelaste ne saura pénétrer en paradis."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ee0bf0b3-f7d9-498f-86f3-55d20cd57f62",
                        "source_entry_id": "7f4a23f1-9099-3b63-b6c8-9d86d811dd17",
                        "source_sense_id": "c46b9801-53c1-3769-a6e0-3a09ea48bfa5",
                        "target_lang_word": "agelast",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "agelast",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "92eb0cc1-1b23-3cb3-b562-6b6e710e7db8",
                                        "entry_id": "0a15bcba-4e87-3208-bc75-716f405c1582",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who never laughs (especially at jokes); a mirthless person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68d8adc3-3505-46d7-9e6c-3c8ede79fec5",
                                                "sense_id": "92eb0cc1-1b23-3cb3-b562-6b6e710e7db8",
                                                "text": "As a real agelast in a comedy, he is beaten. The beating of an agelast is the most important point of the comedy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "264a2329-e954-4dd1-a994-4bccb7c63369",
                                                "sense_id": "92eb0cc1-1b23-3cb3-b562-6b6e710e7db8",
                                                "text": "Declaring with Doumergue that \"Rabelais and Calvin (and Olivétan) were the creators of French literary prose,\"²⁵ Bakhtin adds \"Even the agelast Calvin wrote a pamphlet about relics with a certain comic overtone.\"²⁶ The single, and unusual word \"agelast\" summarizes the popular view of John Calvin: a person who does not laugh or smile; someone who cannot enjoy life or the fact that others might be happy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25c8cae8-fae6-48a4-95c3-4d8566f9abef",
                                                "sense_id": "92eb0cc1-1b23-3cb3-b562-6b6e710e7db8",
                                                "text": "For Kundera, agelasts represent the opposite of the spirit of the novel; the novel is born from the sense of humor and not from theoretical thinking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e21ded6d-39c2-425c-9445-e7590b66b31a",
                                                "sense_id": "92eb0cc1-1b23-3cb3-b562-6b6e710e7db8",
                                                "text": "Agelasts have a very clear idea that they have patent regarding both the truth and the mission and are so bloody solemn that they just cannot accept other views."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
